From: Mobarchy
Subject: [PATCH] devmon_if: no indications with the display off

The indication filter was set to all whatever the display: the modem woke the phone
from deep sleep every few seconds with signal strength and network state reports.
With the display off it is now set to none, as Android's DeviceStateMonitor does.

diff --git a/src/binder_devmon_if.c b/src/binder_devmon_if.c
index 695e309..56c357f 100644
--- a/src/binder_devmon_if.c
+++ b/src/binder_devmon_if.c
@@ -187,8 +187,16 @@ binder_devmon_if_io_set_indication_filter(
          * IRadioNetwork.aidl:
          * void setIndicationFilter(in int serial, in int indicationFilter);
          */
-        DBG_(self, "Setting indication filter: 0x%02x", api->ind_filter_all);
-        gbinder_writer_append_int32(&args, api->ind_filter_all);
+        /*
+         * With the display off, none (as Android does): no signal strength, network
+         * state, dormancy, link capacity... reports to wake the system up for. Calls
+         * and messages are not filtered by this.
+         */
+        const RADIO_IND_FILTER filter = self->display_on ?
+            api->ind_filter_all : (RADIO_IND_FILTER)0;
+
+        DBG_(self, "Setting indication filter: 0x%02x", filter);
+        gbinder_writer_append_int32(&args, filter);
         radio_request_drop(self->req);
         self->req = radio_request_try_submit(req);
     }
